IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Carriage by Air Act 1988 (Singapore) -- what the Act and the three Warsaw texts it gives the force of law (s 3) mean
-- for an air passenger: whether the Convention governs the journey (Art 1, s 10), when the carrier is liable for death,
-- injury, baggage and delay (Arts 17 to 21, s 5, s 9), the limits of liability and when the carrier loses them (Arts 3, 4,
-- 22, 25, s 6(1)), costs (Art 22(4)), void clauses (Art 23), the employee's limits (Art 25A), complaints about baggage
-- (Art 26, s 7), the two-year time bar (Art 29, s 8(1), (4)), where to sue (Art 28) and whom to sue on a journey with
-- successive carriers (Art 30).
--
-- SEAT: the passenger (and, where the passenger has died, those claiming for the death -- s 5).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, version in force from 1/4/2022, as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/CAA1988.txt (SSO, in force as at 2026-09-30).
--
-- The three texts: the Second Schedule is the original Warsaw Convention (1929); the First Schedule is that Convention
-- as amended by the Hague Protocol (1955); the Third Schedule is the Warsaw (Hague) Convention as amended by Montreal
-- Protocol No. 4 (1975). Which text governs a given journey is asked as a fact: the Act says only that each applies to
-- the carriage to which it applies "(as the case may require)" (s 3(1)).
--
-- NOT ENCODED: cargo, air waybills and the consignor's and consignee's rights (Arts 5 to 16, 18 and 22 for cargo);
-- postal carriage and State carriage under the Additional Protocol (Art 2, s 4(1)(e), s 11); the treaty machinery
-- (Arts 36 to 41); combined carriage (Art 31); successive-carrier recourse; contribution between wrongdoers (s 8(2), (3));
-- the court's powers in parallel proceedings beyond the aggregate (s 6(2), (3)); the conversion of francs into
-- Singapore dollars (Art 22(4) Second, Art 22(5) and (6) First and Third, s 6(4): no Minister's order under s 6(4) is deposited, so every limit here is
-- in francs, as the Schedules state it); regulations under s 12; s 13.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the seat of the
-- individual to whom the law is applied, with the design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Carriage by Air Act 1988 -- the passenger`

-- "the Warsaw Convention" (s 2): the 1929 text, Second Schedule.
-- "the Warsaw (Hague) Convention" (s 2): as amended at the Hague, First Schedule.
-- "the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention" (s 2): as further amended by Montreal Protocol No. 4, Third Schedule.
DECLARE `Warsaw text` IS ONE OF
    `the Warsaw Convention`
    `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention`
    `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention`

§§ `Article 1 and section 10 -- does the Convention govern my journey`

-- Art 1(1): "This Convention applies to all international carriage of persons, baggage or cargo performed by aircraft
-- for reward. It applies equally to gratuitous carriage by aircraft performed by an air transport undertaking."
-- Art 1(2): "international carriage" means carriage in which, "according to the agreement between the parties", the
-- place of departure and the place of destination "are situated either within the territories of two High Contracting
-- Parties or within the territory of a single High Contracting Party if there is an agreed stopping place within the
-- territory of another State, even if that State is not a High Contracting Party" (the Second Schedule says "another
-- Power, even though that Power is not a party"; the test is the same).
-- s 4(1): a High Contracting Party is "a country that has ratified or acceded to" the text in question -- asked as a fact.
-- s 10(2): the Warsaw (Hague) and Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Conventions "do not apply to the carriage of persons, cargo
-- and baggage for the military authorities of a State to which this section applies in aircraft registered in that
-- State if the whole capacity of the aircraft has been reserved by or on behalf of those authorities". Section 10 does
-- not name the Warsaw Convention.
DECLARE `My journey` HAS
    `carried by aircraft`                                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `for reward`                                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `free, by an air transport undertaking`                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `departure is in a High Contracting Party`                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `destination is in a High Contracting Party`                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `departure and destination are in the same party`              IS A BOOLEAN
    `there is an agreed stopping place in another State`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `carried for the military of a State named under section 10`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the aircraft is registered in that State`                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `the military reserved the whole aircraft`                     IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the journey` IS A `My journey`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my journey international carriage` IF
        `the journey`'s `departure is in a High Contracting Party`
    AND `the journey`'s `destination is in a High Contracting Party`
    AND (    NOT `the journey`'s `departure and destination are in the same party`
         OR  `the journey`'s `there is an agreed stopping place in another State`)

GIVEN `the text` IS A `Warsaw text`, `the journey` IS A `My journey`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the Convention govern my journey` IF
        `Is my journey international carriage` `the journey`
    AND `the journey`'s `carried by aircraft`
    AND (`the journey`'s `for reward` OR `the journey`'s `free, by an air transport undertaking`)
    AND NOT `excluded as military carriage`
    WHERE
        `excluded as military carriage` MEANS
                CONSIDER `the text`
                WHEN `the Warsaw Convention` THEN FALSE
                OTHERWISE TRUE
            AND `the journey`'s `carried for the military of a State named under section 10`
            AND `the journey`'s `the aircraft is registered in that State`
            AND `the journey`'s `the military reserved the whole aircraft`

§§ `Articles 17 to 20 -- is the carrier liable to me`

-- Art 17: the carrier is liable for damage sustained in the event of "the death or wounding of a passenger or any other
-- bodily injury" if "the accident which caused the damage so sustained took place on board the aircraft or in the
-- course of any of the operations of embarking or disembarking".
-- Art 18(1), (2): liable for "destruction or loss of, or of damage to, any registered baggage" if the occurrence took
-- place "during the carriage by air", which "comprises the period during which the baggage ... is in charge of the
-- carrier". (3): carriage by land, sea or river outside an aerodrome is not carriage by air, but if it is "for the
-- purpose of loading, delivery or transhipment" under the air contract, damage "is presumed, subject to proof to the
-- contrary", to have happened during the carriage by air.
-- Art 19: liable for "damage occasioned by delay in the carriage by air of passengers, baggage or cargo".
-- Art 20 (First Schedule; Art 20(1) Second; Art 20 Third "In the carriage of passengers and baggage"): "The carrier is
-- not liable if he proves that he and his servants and agents have taken all necessary measures to avoid the damage or
-- that it was impossible for him and them to take such measures."
-- Art 20(2), Second Schedule only: "In the carriage of cargo and baggage the carrier is not liable if he proves that the
-- damage was occasioned by negligent pilotage or negligence in the handling of the aircraft or in navigation and that,
-- in all other respects, he and his agents have taken all necessary measures to avoid the damage."
DECLARE `What happened` IS ONE OF
    `I was killed or injured`
    `my checked baggage was destroyed, lost or damaged`
    `I was delayed`
    `my baggage was delayed`

DECLARE `The occurrence` HAS
    `what happened`                                                IS A `What happened`
    `it happened on board or while embarking or disembarking`      IS A BOOLEAN
    `my baggage was in the carrier's charge when it happened`      IS A BOOLEAN
    `it happened on surface transport for loading, delivery or transhipment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the carrier proved it happened outside the carriage by air`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the carrier proved all necessary measures, or that they were impossible` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the carrier proved negligent pilotage, handling or navigation and otherwise all measures` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the text` IS A `Warsaw text`, `the occurrence` IS A `The occurrence`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the carrier liable to me` IF
        `a head of liability is made out`
    AND NOT `the occurrence`'s `the carrier proved all necessary measures, or that they were impossible`
    AND NOT `the pilotage defence succeeds`
    WHERE
        `during the carriage by air` MEANS
                `the occurrence`'s `my baggage was in the carrier's charge when it happened`
            OR  (    `the occurrence`'s `it happened on surface transport for loading, delivery or transhipment`
                 AND NOT `the occurrence`'s `the carrier proved it happened outside the carriage by air`)
        `a head of liability is made out` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the occurrence`'s `what happened`
            WHEN `I was killed or injured` THEN `the occurrence`'s `it happened on board or while embarking or disembarking`
            WHEN `my checked baggage was destroyed, lost or damaged` THEN `during the carriage by air`
            OTHERWISE TRUE
        `the pilotage defence succeeds` MEANS
                CONSIDER `the text`
                WHEN `the Warsaw Convention` THEN TRUE
                OTHERWISE FALSE
            AND CONSIDER `the occurrence`'s `what happened`
                WHEN `my checked baggage was destroyed, lost or damaged` THEN TRUE
                OTHERWISE FALSE
            AND `the occurrence`'s `the carrier proved negligent pilotage, handling or navigation and otherwise all measures`

§§ `Section 5 -- if I die`

-- s 5: "References in section 20 of the Civil Law Act 1909 to a wrongful act, neglect or default include references to
-- any occurrence which gives rise to liability under Article 17 in the First, Second and Third Schedules."
-- What a claim under s 20 of the Civil Law Act 1909 yields is that Act's question, not this one's.
GIVEN `the text` IS A `Warsaw text`, `the occurrence` IS A `The occurrence`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `If I die, does the accident count as a wrongful act for a fatal accidents claim` IF
        CONSIDER `the occurrence`'s `what happened`
        WHEN `I was killed or injured` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE
    AND `Is the carrier liable to me` `the text` `the occurrence`

§§ `Article 21 and section 9 -- my own negligence`

-- Art 21 (Art 21(1) Third, "In the carriage of passengers and baggage"): "If the carrier proves that the damage was
-- caused by or contributed to by the negligence of the injured person the court may, in accordance with the provisions
-- of its own law, exonerate the carrier wholly or partly from his liability."
-- s 9: the Contributory Negligence and Personal Injuries Act 1953 is that law. How much the court takes off is a judgment
-- handed to the court, so the answer is what the court may do, never by how much.
DECLARE `Effect of my negligence` IS ONE OF
    `the court may relieve the carrier wholly or partly`
    `no reduction on this ground`

GIVEN `the carrier proved my negligence caused or contributed to the damage` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Effect of my negligence`
DECIDE `Can my own negligence reduce what I recover` IS
    IF `the carrier proved my negligence caused or contributed to the damage`
    THEN `the court may relieve the carrier wholly or partly`
    ELSE `no reduction on this ground`

§§ `Articles 3, 4, 22 and 25 -- the most I can recover`

-- Art 22(1): "In the carriage of persons the liability of the carrier for each passenger is limited to the sum of"
-- 125,000 francs (Second Schedule) or 250,000 francs (First and Third). "Nevertheless, by special contract, the carrier
-- and the passenger may agree to a higher limit of liability."
-- Art 22(2): for registered baggage, 250 francs per kilogramme in all three, unless a special declaration was made when
-- the package was handed over and any supplementary sum paid; then "a sum not exceeding the declared sum, unless he
-- proves that that sum is greater than" the actual value (Second) or actual interest in delivery (First, Third).
-- Art 22(2)(b) First, 22(2)(c) Third: on loss, damage or delay of part of the baggage the weight is "only the total
-- weight of the package or packages concerned", but other packages on the same baggage check whose value is affected
-- are "also ... taken into consideration". The Second Schedule has no such paragraph.
-- Art 22(3): "As regards objects of which the passenger takes charge himself the liability of the carrier is limited to
-- 5,000 francs per passenger" (all three).
--
-- When the carrier loses the limits:
-- Art 3(2) Second: "if the carrier accepts a passenger without a passenger ticket having been delivered he shall not be
-- entitled to avail himself of those provisions of this Convention which exclude or limit his liability".
-- Art 3(2) First and Third: "if, with the consent of the carrier, the passenger embarks without a passenger ticket
-- having been delivered, or if the ticket does not include the notice required by paragraph (1)(c)", the carrier
-- "shall not be entitled to avail himself of the provisions of Article 22" -- the whole Article, baggage limits included.
-- Art 4(4) Second: baggage accepted "without a baggage check having been delivered, or if the baggage check does not
-- contain the particulars set out at (d) [ticket number], (f) [number and weight of the packages] and (h) [statement
-- that the carriage is subject to the Convention's liability rules]" -- the limits are lost.
-- Art 4(2) First and Third: "if the carrier takes charge of the baggage without a baggage check having been delivered
-- or if the baggage check (unless combined with or incorporated in the passenger ticket which complies with the
-- provisions of Article 3, paragraph (1)(c)) does not include the notice", the carrier loses "Article 22, paragraph (2)".
-- Art 25 Second: the limits go "if the damage is caused by his wilful misconduct or by such default on his part as, in
-- accordance with the law of the court seised of the case, is considered to be equivalent to wilful misconduct", or by
-- a servant or agent "acting within the scope of his employment". The court's finding is an input.
-- Art 25 First (Third: "In the carriage of passengers and baggage"): the limits "shall not apply if it is proved that
-- the damage resulted from an act or omission of the carrier, his servants or agents, done with intent to cause damage
-- or recklessly and with knowledge that damage would probably result", a servant or agent "acting within the scope of
-- his employment".
DECLARE `What I claim for` IS ONE OF
    `my death or injury`
    `delay to me`
    `my checked baggage`
    `things I kept with me`

DECLARE `My claim` HAS
    `the governing text`                                           IS A `Warsaw text`
    `what I claim for`                                             IS A `What I claim for`
    `I was given a ticket`                                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `the carrier let me board`                                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `my ticket carries the Warsaw notice`                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `I was given a baggage check`                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `my baggage check carries the Warsaw notice`                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `my baggage check is part of a ticket carrying the notice`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `my baggage check shows my ticket number`                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `my baggage check shows the number and weight of my bags`      IS A BOOLEAN
    `my baggage check states the Convention liability rules`       IS A BOOLEAN
    `the court finds wilful misconduct or its equivalent`          IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is proved the damage was done with intent or recklessly with knowledge` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the higher limit agreed by special contract`                  IS A NUMBER
    `I declared my interest in delivery and paid any supplement`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the sum I declared`                                           IS A NUMBER
    `the carrier proved my declared sum exceeds my actual interest` IS A BOOLEAN
    `my actual interest in delivery`                               IS A NUMBER
    `kilogrammes of the packages concerned`                        IS A NUMBER
    `kilogrammes of other packages on the same check whose value is affected` IS A NUMBER

-- The answer. "francs" (Art 22(5) First and Third; Art 22(4) Second): a unit of 65 1/2 milligrammes of gold of millesimal
-- fineness 900. No order under s 6(4) is deposited, so no Singapore-dollar figure is given.
DECLARE `The most I can recover` IS ONE OF
    `no Convention limit applies`
    `limited to francs` HAS `francs` IS A NUMBER
    `not covered by this encoding`

GIVEN `the claim` IS A `My claim`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has the carrier lost the right to limit what it pays me` IF
    CONSIDER `the claim`'s `the governing text`
    WHEN `the Warsaw Convention` THEN
            `boarded without a ticket`
        OR  `the claim`'s `the court finds wilful misconduct or its equivalent`
        OR  (`a baggage claim` AND `the 1929 baggage check is defective`)
    OTHERWISE
            `boarded without a ticket`
        OR  (`the claim`'s `I was given a ticket` AND NOT `the claim`'s `my ticket carries the Warsaw notice`)
        OR  `the claim`'s `it is proved the damage was done with intent or recklessly with knowledge`
        OR  (`a baggage claim` AND `the amended baggage check is defective`)
    WHERE
        `boarded without a ticket` MEANS
            `the claim`'s `the carrier let me board` AND NOT `the claim`'s `I was given a ticket`
        `a baggage claim` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the claim`'s `what I claim for`
            WHEN `my checked baggage` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE
        `the 1929 baggage check is defective` MEANS
                NOT `the claim`'s `I was given a baggage check`
            OR  NOT `the claim`'s `my baggage check shows my ticket number`
            OR  NOT `the claim`'s `my baggage check shows the number and weight of my bags`
            OR  NOT `the claim`'s `my baggage check states the Convention liability rules`
        `the amended baggage check is defective` MEANS
                NOT `the claim`'s `I was given a baggage check`
            OR  (    NOT `the claim`'s `my baggage check carries the Warsaw notice`
                 AND NOT `the claim`'s `my baggage check is part of a ticket carrying the notice`)

GIVEN `the claim` IS A `My claim`
GIVETH A `The most I can recover`
DECIDE `What is the most I can recover` IS
    IF `Has the carrier lost the right to limit what it pays me` `the claim`
    THEN `no Convention limit applies`
    ELSE CONSIDER `the claim`'s `what I claim for`
         WHEN `my death or injury` THEN `limited to francs` `the passenger limit`
         -- INFERENCE: delay to the passenger falls under "the liability of the carrier for each passenger" (Art 22(1));
         -- Art 22 names no other limit for it.
         WHEN `delay to me` THEN `limited to francs` `the passenger limit`
         WHEN `things I kept with me` THEN `limited to francs` 5000
         WHEN `my checked baggage` THEN `the baggage limit`
    WHERE
        `the treaty passenger limit` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the claim`'s `the governing text`
            WHEN `the Warsaw Convention` THEN 125000
            OTHERWISE 250000
        `the passenger limit` MEANS
            IF `the claim`'s `the higher limit agreed by special contract` GREATER THAN `the treaty passenger limit`
            THEN `the claim`'s `the higher limit agreed by special contract`
            ELSE `the treaty passenger limit`
        -- INFERENCE: where the carrier proves the declared sum exceeds the actual value or interest, the limit is that
        -- actual value or interest.
        -- READING: the Second Schedule's Art 22(2) speaks of a declaration by "the consignor"; Art 4(3)(g) of the same
        -- text puts "the amount of the value declared in accordance with Article 22(2)" on the passenger's baggage
        -- check, so the passenger's declaration is taken to count. See NOTES.md.
        `the declared limit` MEANS
            IF `the claim`'s `the carrier proved my declared sum exceeds my actual interest`
            THEN `limited to francs` (`the claim`'s `my actual interest in delivery`)
            ELSE `limited to francs` (`the claim`'s `the sum I declared`)
        `the baggage limit` MEANS
            IF `the claim`'s `I declared my interest in delivery and paid any supplement`
            THEN `the declared limit`
            ELSE CONSIDER `the claim`'s `the governing text`
                 -- The Second Schedule has no rule on the weight to count when other packages are affected; INFERENCE:
                 -- otherwise the weight is that of the baggage lost, damaged or delayed.
                 WHEN `the Warsaw Convention` THEN
                    IF `the claim`'s `kilogrammes of other packages on the same check whose value is affected` GREATER THAN 0
                    THEN `not covered by this encoding`
                    ELSE `limited to francs` (250 TIMES `the claim`'s `kilogrammes of the packages concerned`)
                 OTHERWISE `limited to francs` (250 TIMES (    `the claim`'s `kilogrammes of the packages concerned`
                                                         PLUS `the claim`'s `kilogrammes of other packages on the same check whose value is affected`))

§§ `Section 6(1) -- one limit across all my proceedings`

-- s 6(1): the Art 22 limits "apply whatever the nature of the proceedings", and "the limitation for each passenger in
-- Article 22(1) ... applies to the aggregate liability of the carrier in all proceedings which may be brought against
-- him under the law of Singapore, together with any proceedings brought against him outside Singapore".
-- s 6(2), (3): the court may make any order that is "just and equitable", award less, or make part of an award
-- conditional on other proceedings -- a judgment for the court, not encoded beyond the aggregate.
GIVEN `the claim` IS A `My claim`, `francs already recovered from the carrier elsewhere` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `The most I can recover`
DECIDE `What is the most I can still recover in these proceedings` IS
    CONSIDER `the claim`'s `what I claim for`
    WHEN `my death or injury` THEN `the remainder`
    WHEN `delay to me` THEN `the remainder`
    -- s 6(1) states the aggregate only for the passenger limit in Art 22(1).
    OTHERWISE `not covered by this encoding`
    WHERE
        `the remainder` MEANS
            CONSIDER `What is the most I can recover` `the claim`
            WHEN `limited to francs` f THEN
                IF f GREATER THAN `francs already recovered from the carrier elsewhere`
                THEN `limited to francs` (f MINUS `francs already recovered from the carrier elsewhere`)
                ELSE `limited to francs` 0
            WHEN `no Convention limit applies` THEN `no Convention limit applies`
            OTHERWISE `not covered by this encoding`

§§ `Article 22(4) -- my costs on top of the limit`

-- Art 22(4) First and Third: "The limits prescribed in this Article shall not prevent the court from awarding, in
-- accordance with its own law, in addition, the whole or part of the court costs and of the other expenses of the
-- litigation incurred by the plaintiff. The foregoing provision shall not apply if the amount of the damages awarded,
-- excluding court costs and other expenses of the litigation, does not exceed the sum which the carrier has offered in
-- writing to the plaintiff within a period of 6 months from the date of the occurrence causing the damage, or before
-- the commencement of the action, if that is later."
-- The Second Schedule's Art 22(4) is about the franc; it has no costs rule.
DECLARE `My costs` IS ONE OF
    `the court may award my costs on top of the limit`
    `Article 22(4) gives no costs on top of the limit`
    `this text has no costs rule`

GIVEN `the text` IS A `Warsaw text`,
      `damages awarded` IS A NUMBER,
      `the carrier made a written offer in time` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the sum the carrier offered in writing` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `My costs`
DECIDE `Can I recover my costs on top of the limit` IS
    CONSIDER `the text`
    WHEN `the Warsaw Convention` THEN `this text has no costs rule`
    OTHERWISE
        IF      `the carrier made a written offer in time`
            AND `damages awarded` AT MOST `the sum the carrier offered in writing`
        THEN `Article 22(4) gives no costs on top of the limit`
        ELSE `the court may award my costs on top of the limit`

§§ `Article 23 -- a clause in my ticket that lowers the limit`

-- Art 23(1): "Any provision tending to relieve the carrier of liability or to fix a lower limit than that which is laid
-- down in this Convention shall be null and void, but the nullity of any such provision does not involve the nullity of
-- the whole contract". (Art 23(2), First and Third, excepts only clauses on the inherent defect of cargo.)
GIVEN `the clause relieves the carrier of liability` IS A BOOLEAN, `the clause fixes a lower limit than the Convention` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the clause in my contract void` IF
    `the clause relieves the carrier of liability` OR `the clause fixes a lower limit than the Convention`

§§ `Article 25A -- suing the carrier's employee`

-- Art 25A(1) First and Third: a servant or agent sued "if he proves that he acted within the scope of his employment,
-- shall be entitled to avail himself of the limits of liability which that carrier himself is entitled to invoke";
-- (2) the aggregate recoverable from carrier, servants and agents "shall not exceed the said limits"; (3) not "if it is
-- proved that the damage resulted from an act or omission of the servant or agent done with intent to cause damage or
-- recklessly and with knowledge that damage would probably result". The Second Schedule has no Article 25A, so it gives
-- the employee no such right.
GIVEN `the text` IS A `Warsaw text`,
      `the employee proved acting within the scope of employment` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `it is proved the employee acted with intent or recklessly with knowledge` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the employee I sue rely on the carrier's limits` IF
        CONSIDER `the text`
        WHEN `the Warsaw Convention` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE
    AND `the employee proved acting within the scope of employment`
    AND NOT `it is proved the employee acted with intent or recklessly with knowledge`

§§ `Article 26 and section 7 -- complaining about my baggage`

-- Art 26(2): "In the case of damage, the person entitled to delivery must complain to the carrier forthwith after the
-- discovery of the damage, and, at the latest, within" 3 days (Second) or 7 days (First, Third) "from the date of
-- receipt in the case of baggage". "In the case of delay the complaint must be made at the latest within" 14 days
-- (Second) or 21 days (First, Third) "from the date on which the baggage ... has been placed at his disposal".
-- (3): "in writing upon the document of carriage or by separate notice in writing despatched within the times
-- aforesaid". (4): "Failing complaint within the times aforesaid, no action shall lie against the carrier, save in the
-- case of fraud on his part."
-- s 7: "damage" includes "loss of part of the baggage", and receipt, for a partial loss, means "receipt of the
-- remainder of it".
DECLARE `My baggage problem` IS ONE OF
    `my bags were damaged`
    `part of my bags was lost`
    `my bags arrived late`
    `my bags never arrived`

-- Days after the date of receipt (damage, partial loss) or after the bags were placed at my disposal (delay).
-- NOTHING: Art 26 sets no complaint period for baggage never received. INFERENCE: with no receipt, Art 26(2) does not
-- start; the text does not say so in terms.
GIVEN `the text` IS A `Warsaw text`, `the problem` IS A `My baggage problem`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the last day I may complain` IS
    CONSIDER `the problem`
    WHEN `my bags were damaged` THEN JUST `damage days`
    WHEN `part of my bags was lost` THEN JUST `damage days`
    WHEN `my bags arrived late` THEN JUST `delay days`
    WHEN `my bags never arrived` THEN NOTHING
    WHERE
        `damage days` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the text`
            WHEN `the Warsaw Convention` THEN 3
            OTHERWISE 7
        `delay days` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the text`
            WHEN `the Warsaw Convention` THEN 14
            OTHERWISE 21

DECLARE `My complaint` IS ONE OF
    `no action lies for want of complaint`
    `my complaint was in time`
    `Article 26 sets no complaint period`

-- READING: "forthwith after the discovery" is part of "the times aforesaid" in Art 26(4). Whether I complained
-- forthwith is a judgment for the court, asked as an input; for delay the text has no "forthwith" limb.
GIVEN `the text` IS A `Warsaw text`,
      `the problem` IS A `My baggage problem`,
      `I complained in writing` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `days after receipt or disposal when I sent it` IS A NUMBER,
      `the court finds I complained forthwith on discovery` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the carrier acted fraudulently` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `My complaint`
DECIDE `Is my baggage claim barred for want of complaint` IS
    CONSIDER `What is the last day I may complain` `the text` `the problem`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `Article 26 sets no complaint period`
    WHEN JUST `last day` THEN
        IF     `the carrier acted fraudulently`
            OR (    `I complained in writing`
                AND `days after receipt or disposal when I sent it` AT MOST `last day`
                AND (`forthwith is not required` OR `the court finds I complained forthwith on discovery`))
        THEN `my complaint was in time`
        ELSE `no action lies for want of complaint`
    WHERE
        `forthwith is not required` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the problem`
            WHEN `my bags arrived late` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `Article 29 and section 8 -- the two years`

-- Art 29(1): "The right to damages shall be extinguished if an action is not brought within two years, reckoned from
-- the date of arrival at the destination, or from the date on which the aircraft ought to have arrived, or from the
-- date on which the carriage stopped." (2): "The method of calculating the period of limitation shall be determined by
-- the law of the court seised of the case."
-- s 8(1): no action against "a carrier's employee or agent" acting "within the scope of his or her employment" is to be
-- brought "after more than 2 years", reckoned from the same dates. s 8(4): "action" includes an arbitration.
-- INFERENCE (Art 29(2) leaves the method to the court): the two years end on the anniversary of the reckoning date,
-- and an action brought on that anniversary is in time. A 29 February reckoning date ends on 28 February.
DECLARE `Whom I sue` IS ONE OF
    `the carrier`
    `the carrier's employee or agent acting in the scope of employment`
    `the carrier's employee or agent acting outside it`

DECLARE `My time` IS ONE OF
    `my action is in time`
    `my right to damages is extinguished`
    `not covered by this encoding`

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`date order of` d MEANS DATE_YEAR d TIMES 10000 PLUS DATE_MONTH d TIMES 100 PLUS DATE_DAY d

GIVEN `whom I sue` IS A `Whom I sue`,
      `the date of arrival, of due arrival, or when the carriage stopped` IS A DATE,
      `the date I brought my action or arbitration` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `My time`
DECIDE `Is my action out of time` IS
    CONSIDER `whom I sue`
    -- Neither Art 29 nor s 8(1) speaks to an employee acting outside the scope of employment.
    WHEN `the carrier's employee or agent acting outside it` THEN `not covered by this encoding`
    OTHERWISE
        IF     `date order of` `the date I brought my action or arbitration`
           AT MOST `date order of` `the date of arrival, of due arrival, or when the carriage stopped` PLUS 20000
        THEN `my action is in time`
        ELSE `my right to damages is extinguished`

§§ `Article 28 -- where I can sue`

-- Art 28(1): "An action for damages must be brought, at the option of the plaintiff, in the territory of one of the
-- High Contracting Parties, either before the court having jurisdiction where the carrier is ordinarily resident, or
-- has his principal place of business, or has an establishment by which the contract has been made or before the court
-- having jurisdiction at the place of destination." (Same in all three texts.)
DECLARE `The court` HAS
    `it is in a High Contracting Party`                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `the carrier is ordinarily resident there`                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `the carrier has its principal place of business there`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `the carrier has the establishment there that made my contract` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is at my place of destination`                             IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the court` IS A `The court`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I sue the carrier in this court` IF
        `the court`'s `it is in a High Contracting Party`
    AND (   `the court`'s `the carrier is ordinarily resident there`
         OR `the court`'s `the carrier has its principal place of business there`
         OR `the court`'s `the carrier has the establishment there that made my contract`
         OR `the court`'s `it is at my place of destination`)

§§ `Article 30 -- whom I can sue when several carriers flew me`

-- Art 30(2): on successive carriage, "the passenger or his representative can take action only against the carrier
-- who performed the carriage during which the accident or the delay occurred, save in the case where, by express
-- agreement, the first carrier has assumed liability for the whole journey".
-- Art 30(3): "As regards baggage ... the passenger ... will have a right of action against the first carrier, and the
-- passenger ... who is entitled to delivery will have a right of action against the last carrier, and further, each
-- may take action against the carrier who performed the carriage during which the destruction, loss, damage or delay
-- took place."
DECLARE `The carrier I would sue` IS ONE OF
    `the carrier who flew the leg where it happened`
    `the first carrier`
    `the last carrier`
    `another carrier on the journey`

GIVEN `what happened` IS A `What happened`,
      `the carrier` IS A `The carrier I would sue`,
      `the first carrier expressly assumed the whole journey` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I sue this carrier` IF
    CONSIDER `the carrier`
    WHEN `the carrier who flew the leg where it happened` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `another carrier on the journey` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the first carrier` THEN `a baggage case` OR `the first carrier expressly assumed the whole journey`
    WHEN `the last carrier` THEN `a baggage case`
    WHERE
        `a baggage case` MEANS
            CONSIDER `what happened`
            WHEN `my checked baggage was destroyed, lost or damaged` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `my baggage was delayed` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE
